<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Oruç Reis</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1474–1518</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as Aruj Barbarossa, Oruç Barbarossa</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Oruç Reis, called Barbarossa, was an Ottoman corsair from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lesbos">Lesbos</a> who, with his brother Hayreddin, raided Spanish shipping and coasts from bases in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-africa">North Africa</a>. He lost an arm attacking Spanish-held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bejaia">Bejaia</a> in 1512, seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/algiers">Algiers</a> in 1516 and made himself its ruler. He was killed by Spanish forces near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tlemcen">Tlemcen</a> in 1518, and Hayreddin then placed Algiers under the Ottoman sultan.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/oruc-reis.jpg" alt="Oruç Reis" width="320" height="384" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Johann Theodor de Bry · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arolsen_Klebeband_01_465_4.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
